  "term": "neurocrine",
  "definition": "Neurocrine refers to control or signaling by substances released from neurons that act on nearby tissues or cells. In this source, vasoactive intestinal peptide is described as a neurocrine factor from enteric neurons that helps regulate intestinal calcium transport.",
