      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence gives a general definition of “neurocrine” (control/signaling by substances released from neurons acting on nearby tissues/cells) that is not explicitly supported in the provided packet text.",
        "While the packet supports that vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP) is described as a “neurocrine factor” released by enteric neurons and that it is involved in regulating intestinal calcium transport (via effects on transepithelial calcium flux), it does not provide the general definitional phrasing used in the first sentence.",
        "The packet explicitly characterizes the evidence about VIP’s role as “postulated” and notes prior evidence is “scant and inconclusive,” so presenting the general concept of neurocrine control as established in the first sentence is not fully defensible from the packet."
